WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.514 --> 00:00:02.180
NICHOLAS HARTEAU: The
mission of Spotify

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.920
is really about being a
great musical companion

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.516
and making it more personal.

00:00:06.516 --> 00:00:08.640
It's not going to be the
streaming music experience

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.950
or the online music experience.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.589
It's going to be your
music experience.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:13.880
SABRINA RABELLO ARONSON: We
create the tools for people

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.830
to actually swim in
that sea of music data

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.150
and find the information
that really corresponds

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.275
to why they're there.

00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:23.900
WOUTER DE BIE: Quite
a while ago, we've

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.624
made a decision
to focus on data.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:27.040
SABRINA RABELLO
ARONSON: Depending

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.310
on the complexity of the query,
it could take a whole day.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.139
Sometimes, it would
have to run overnight.

00:00:32.139 --> 00:00:34.430
WOUTER DE BIE: And being able
to store that and process

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.420
that has been a
very big challenge.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.320
Moving to Google's
Cloud Platform

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.670
enabled us to take use of the
scale that Google can provide.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.670
NICHOLAS HARTEAU: The
reality is it's quite hard

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.280
to build great data centers.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.540
And we saw an opportunity to
spend our focus elsewhere.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.309
And that was really the driver
into Google's Cloud Platform.

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:53.350
SABRINA RABELLO ARONSON:
With Google Cloud tools,

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.130
we can rerun the same query.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.045
And it might take a
few seconds, minutes.

00:00:57.045 --> 00:00:58.670
NICHOLAS HARTEAU:
The less time that we

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.400
can spend solving
problems that are already

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.670
solved, like scaling
our Hadoop cluster

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.360
when Google has
already figured out

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.440
how to scale it for us,
the more time and energy

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.290
we can spend on turning
our data into value.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.027
And that's really a
game-changer for us.

00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:13.610
When you're talking
about a technology

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.120
like BigQuery, when you're
talking about Dataflow,

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.180
you will feel the Spotify
product evolve, making the user

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.020
experience great.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.270
SABRINA RABELLO ARONSON:
Once you break down the data,

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.400
you realize that
there are nuances.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.000
It's not a straightforward path.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.100
It's a mosaic rich beyond
the most popular artists.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.970
It's a lot more than that.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.370
Music can transcend boundaries
of language, culture.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.420
If it moves you,
then it's there.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.850
And it's there forever.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.900
[MUSIC PLAYING]

